  <section class="page-header">
    <h1>Living in Andorra</h1>
    <p>
      A small sovereign country in the Pyrenees. The luxury is space, air and a
      short list of neighbours — not a resort performance.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <h2>Scale</h2>
    <p>
      Andorra is a co-principality between France and Spain. You can drive the
      main valley in well under an hour. That compactness is the point: a
      working capital, ski parishes, and high villages share one set of
      institutions.
    </p>
    <p>
      It is not a suburb of Barcelona or Toulouse. Catalan is the official
      language; Spanish and French are widely used; English is common in
      professional rooms and less so in the village shop. New residents are
      expected, on current Government notes, to move towards Catalan at renewal.
      Confirm the level then required on
      <a href="https://www.govern.ad/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
        >Govern.ad</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2>A year in the mountains</h2>
    <p>
      Winter is the public season: Grandvalira on the eastern side, Pal-Arinsal
      and Arcalís in the west. The slopes are close to the villages, which is
      why the country feels different from a long-transfer Alpine resort.
    </p>
    <p>
      Summer is quieter and, for many residents, better. High trails, the
      Madriu-Perafita-Claror cultural landscape, Sorteny and Comapedrosa are the
      outdoor architecture of the place. Autumn is short and clear; spring is
      the melt.
    </p>

    <h2>Where to live</h2>
    <p>
      The seven parishes are the real map. Andorra la Vella and Escaldes-Engordany
      hold most appointments and the public hospital. Ordino and Canillo are
      higher and slower. La Massana and Encamp sit on ski roads. Sant Julià de
      Lòria is the southern gate, closer to Spain and the university.
    </p>
    <p>
      Read the
      <a href="/parishes">parish notes</a>
      before you ask an agent to search. Housing suitable for a residence file
      is not the same as a holiday chalet. See
      <a href="/properties">properties</a>
      for how we will list homes, and
      <a href="/directory">the directory</a>
      for AGIA-registered agents.
    </p>

    <h2>Schools and health</h2>
    <p>
      Education is plural. Govern.ad publishes three coexisting systems —
      Andorran, Spanish and French — and a Formació Andorrana course so that
      Catalan and Andorran institutions are taught in the non-Andorran schools.
      The public university sits in Sant Julià de Lòria. We set this out, with
      the official links, on
      <a href="/education">education</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Public healthcare is organised by
      <a href="https://saas.ad/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SAAS</a>, which
      describes Hospital Nostra Senyora de Meritxell as the country’s only
      hospital and runs primary-care centres in the parishes. Social security is
      <a href="https://www.cass.ad/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CASS</a>.
      Coverage depends on affiliation, not on a marketing line. Read
      <a href="/healthcare">healthcare</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Money and paper</h2>
    <p>
      Daily banking is local. The Association of Andorran Banks lists three
      groups:
      <a href="/directory/andbank">Andbank</a>,
      <a href="/directory/morabanc">MoraBanc</a>
      and
      <a href="/directory/creand">Creand</a>. Opening an account is a compliance
      process, not a formality. The supervisor is the
      <a href="https://www.afa.ad/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">AFA</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Jane Whittaker publishes
      <a
        href="http://www.livinginandorra.com/files/COST_2025.pdf"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">itemised cost estimates</a
      >
      on livinginandorra.com. Those figures are hers, not official prices.
      Driving-licence photograph and signature are taken at Government
      premises on the
      <a
        href="https://www.e-tramits.ad/tramits/renovacio-del-permis-de-conduir/p/GV000303"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">official e-tramits pages</a
      >. Border conditions under the European Entry/Exit System are on
      <a href="/practitioner-map">the practitioner map</a>
      — only the Govern.ad text, not her queue notes.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you are moving, start with
      <a href="/become-a-resident">become a resident</a>
      and the official immigration pages —
      <a href="/residence-without-work">D.1</a>,
      <a href="/family-reunification">B.1</a>,
      <a href="/tax-residence">tax residence</a>.
      The registers themselves are collected on
      <a href="/official-sources">official sources</a>.
      If you want an introduction, use the form on the residency page or write
      to
      <a href="mailto:hello@privateandorra.com">hello@privateandorra.com</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
